cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QuantOS: a quantitative research platform built from first principles"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Boulan
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielboulan10/QuantOS"
url: "https://danielboulan10.github.io/QuantOS/"
abstract: >-
  A quantitative research platform whose numerical core is implemented from first
  principles with NumPy as its only runtime dependency: special functions,
  statistical tests, optimisers, a limit order book with an optional C++ backend,
  an agent-based market simulation, derivatives pricing and volatility surface
  fitting, microstructure estimators, and simulated forward distributions whose
  probabilities are calibration-tested. Validation is adversarial by design --
  deflated Sharpe ratios, purged cross-validation, probability of backtest
  overfitting, and an append-only forward-testing ledger that records predictions
  before their outcomes exist.
keywords:
  - quantitative-finance
  - market-microstructure
  - limit-order-book
  - volatility-forecasting
  - backtest-overfitting
  - numerical-methods
license: MIT
